  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Scientific Research obligated $314M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 91 awards, with an average award size of $3.5M. Scientific Research obligations are down 36.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year run that peaked at $498M in FY25 and declined to $314M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $268M for Scientific Research work so far in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is the largest market for Scientific Research, with $236M obligated in that NAICS category. The General Services Administration obligated $41.1M and the Department of State obligated $4.9M to Scientific Research in FY2026 to date. Other smaller markets for Scientific Research include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $19.4M and Other Computer Related Services at $6.6M. The dataset notes current-year totals are partial and that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Scientific Research’s biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the largest federal customer for Scientific Research, with $268M obligated in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration is the second-largest buyer, with $41.1M obligated. Department of State is a distant third at $4.9M, followed by Department of Transportation at $673K and Department of Homeland Security at $58.8K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What products and services does Scientific Research sell to the government?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the primary product/service area for Scientific Research, with $236M obligated in FY2026 to date. Scientific Research also provides All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $51M and specialized manufacturing and systems work such as Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $19.4M. Smaller obligations include Other Computer Related Services at $6.6M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $1.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
